Title: "Relation"
Id: "4ed9df33-7da1-4263-b1ef-d7a6ad578912"

Text: "`Relation:` states a bidirectional relationship between the two subjects named
in `between:` and `and:`. It is a heading-less, standalone descriptive item and
does not register a build or view rule.

```mlg-fragment
Relation: <OpenText>*
using?: <DeclarationStatement>+
between: <RelationSubject>
and: <RelationSubject>
when?: <ClauseUnion>+
specifies?: <RelationSpecifies>
Documented?: <DocumentedItemUnion>+
Justification?: <HaveGroup>+
Aliases?: <AliasItemUnion>+
Writing?: \"<WritingAlias>\"+
References?: <ResourceHeader>+
Metadata?: <MetadataItemUnion>+
Id?: <OpenText>
```

`Relation:` takes no bracket heading. `between:` and `and:` are required. Each
subject is either an unquoted declaration such as `a is \real` for a concept, or
a quoted reference — a `\"#topic\"` or a `\"\signature\"` (a `\command` with its
arguments removed, such as `\function:on:to`) — so a `Relation:` may relate
concepts, topics, and definitions in any combination. `specifies:` is likewise
either an unquoted clause or quoted prose.

```mlg-fragment
Relation:
between: \"#real.analysis\"
and: \"\sin\"
specifies: \"The sine function is studied within real analysis.\"
```

```mlg-fragment
Relation:
using:
. n is \integer
between: a is \real
and: b is \real
when:
. a = b
specifies: a = b
Documented:
. description: \"a and b name the same value.\"
```

The item is checked like a theorem: declaration subjects and a statement
`specifies:` are validated for declared symbols and valid command references,
while quoted-text references and prose `specifies:` are recorded rather than
proven."
Id: "f061cb10-9022-43ed-8162-7286b9958c3d"
